From 0097cabcad78a9cf0c0247bbd64ac7f350be04aa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Season Tempo Build <claude@seasontempo.local>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 12:37:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Transaction Budget Line: show available lines immediately,
 not after typing

Clicking Budget Line in Add/Edit Transaction opened a search box with nothing
under it. Every line existed, but none of them would show until you typed a
character, so you had to already know what a budget line was called before
you could pick it.

The picker component (SearchPicker, shared by several fields in the app) has
two ways to show items: a filtered list once you start typing, and a
'suggested' list meant to show something before you type. Every other field
that uses this picker passes something into 'suggested'. The Transaction
Budget Line field never did, so it had nothing to show until search kicked
in.

It now passes the season's budget lines into that existing slot, split by
Expense/Income to match what you'd end up picking anyway. Typing still
narrows the list exactly as before. The message under an empty list now says
there are no budget lines yet, instead of telling you to start typing.

Nothing else about the field changed. Selecting a line still only ever picks
a real budget line -- there is still no way to type something in and have it
saved as a budget line directly. Add, Edit, and reassigning a line from the
Budget delete blocked screen all use this same field, so all three are fixed
together.

Season Tempo QA: ST-004.
---
 components/FinanceClient.js | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/components/FinanceClient.js b/components/FinanceClient.js
index 444bc4c..80478c5 100644
--- a/components/FinanceClient.js
+++ b/components/FinanceClient.js
@@ -1754,13 +1754,22 @@ function TransactionForm({ row, budgetItems, tournaments, players, facilities, p
                   ...b,
                   searchText: `${b.name} ${b.category}`,
                 }))}
+                /* ST-004: shown immediately when the picker opens, before any
+                   typing — a coach shouldn't have to already know a budget
+                   line's name to see what exists. `suggested` is the picker's
+                   existing pre-search slot (used elsewhere for likely
+                   matches); typing still narrows the list via `matches`,
+                   computed separately from `items` above, so search behavior
+                   is unchanged. */
+                suggested={eligibleLines}
+                suggestedLabel={isIncome ? "Income budget lines" : "Expense budget lines"}
                 renderItem={(b) => (
                   <>
                     <span className="picker-item-name">{b.name}</span>
                     <span className="picker-item-meta">{b.category}</span>
                   </>
                 )}
-                emptyHint="Start typing to search your budget lines."
+                emptyHint={`No ${isIncome ? "income" : "expense"} budget lines exist yet for this season.`}
                 createLabel="+ Add budget line"
                 onSelect={(b) => {
                   setBudgetItemId(b.id);
-- 
